<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kuto Besak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1797">1797</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Benteng Kuto Besak</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kuto Besak is a walled brick palace-fortress (kraton) on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musi-river">Musi River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palembang">Palembang</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, completed in 1797 for the Sultanate of Palembang. It served as the residence of the sultans until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> conquest in 1821, after which it was used as a military fort; it still stands near the Great Mosque.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kuto-besak.jpg" alt="Kuto Besak" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arisdp · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kutobesak.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
